{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgANyGH9vyDpXeB89NBkB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged()`. It sets the receiver's seen version to the channel's current version, so the current value counts as seen without being borrowed. It sits right after `mark_changed()` in `tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`, with the same style of doc comment.\n\n**What changed:**\n- `tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`: the new method, 11 lines.\n- `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`: a new test, `rx_mark_unchanged`. It checks that the method undoes `mark_changed()`, after which `changed()` waits instead of returning. It also checks that after a `send`, `has_changed()` returns false but `borrow_and_update()` still returns the new value.\n\n**Checks run:**\n- The new test failed to compile before the method existed and passes now.\n- All 10 tests in `sync_watch` pass, and the 18 doctests in `sync::watch` pass.\n- `cargo fmt --check` is clean.\n- Clippy reports no warnings on the new lines. The only warnings in `watch.rs` are the existing `loom` cfg ones.\n\nThe method works the same if the sender has already been dropped: it just records the version. If a value is sent right after the call, `has_changed()` still returns true, as it should.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":961,"cache_read_input_tokens":38125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":961,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7157f50d-41ce-483b-bfbd-c8d661bad7d3","uuid":"7f1a47e1-0467-4b50-baac-8debadb46400","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:03:27.384Z","request_id":"req_011CgANyG31RmBRFsQnzLWt7"}
